E AX3049 1010-unsafe-primitives.ax:19:6-13 restriction-violated "`retains` claims `restrict(no-unsafe)` and the body performs Unsafe: retains -> __retain" ^-:"__retain" ?"a restriction is a CLAIM the author wrote, and this is the compiler answering it. `no-io`, `no-alloc`, `no-unsafe`, `no-foreign`, `no-cast:deep` and `no-recursion` are transitive - the effect row and the call graph are fixpoints over every callee - and the path in the message is the chain of resolved calls (`symbols --calls` spells each hop the same way) from this declaration to where the effect enters, or around the cycle, so the fix is at a named place rather than somewhere below. Make the body keep the claim, or delete the tag, which WITHDRAWS the claim rather than answering it; an unrestricted function is never asked"
E AX3073 1010-unsafe-primitives.ax:21:6-14 undeclared-unsafe "`retains` touches raw memory and its declaration does not say so" #"__retain" ?19:1:"write `;@axiom:effect(unsafe)` above the declaration"~>";@axiom:effect(unsafe)\n" ?"this fires where the unsafe operation is performed, not up the call chain. The tag alone makes the declaration a trusted encapsulation, whose callers inherit nothing; write `;@axiom:precondition(...)` beside it as well when its safety depends on what its caller passes. If the operation is not wanted here the fix is to stop performing it, not to stop saying so"
